diff --git a/docs/reference/boot-configuration.md b/docs/reference/boot-configuration.md
index 947d9f0..8ac7b7c 100644
--- a/docs/reference/boot-configuration.md
+++ b/docs/reference/boot-configuration.md
@@ -2,6 +2,13 @@
 
 The UniXNU boot manager reads `\EFI\UniXNU\unixnu.toml` from the volume it was started from, then from every other volume. A kit directory contains `Kit.toml` with the same match and injection sections.
 
+A firmware environment selector may launch UniXNU with the exact UTF-16 load
+option `unixnu:selected-payload`. In that mode the configuration must come from
+the loaded image's own device handle and must parse without error. A missing,
+invalid or fallback-volume configuration returns failure before publishing
+slices, injecting drivers or starting a kernel. Ordinary application and
+firmware launches keep the existing discovery behavior.
+
 Boot arguments are stored in the payload's `EFI/UniXNU/unixnu.toml`. After changing them, run `./unixnu payload` and `./unixnu bootimg`, then boot the new image. See [apply boot arguments](/xnu/boot-arguments#apply-arguments) for precedence and inspection commands.
 
 ## Procedure {#procedure}
